WEBVTT

00:28:58.150 --> 00:29:01.945
You gather a group of people, ideally
from different parts of your organization,

00:29:01.969 --> 00:29:05.520
and ask them to pair up with someone
they barely know or don't know at all.

00:29:05.544 --> 00:29:08.895
They take turns trying to form
a high-quality connection in that moment

00:29:08.919 --> 00:29:10.070
with one another.

00:29:10.094 --> 00:29:13.238
They don't get any directions,
and they only have one minute each.

00:29:13.262 --> 00:29:15.906
JD: And it's unbelievable what happens.

00:29:15.930 --> 00:29:21.666
I mean, it's so great because the energy
of the room just like -- voom!

00:29:21.690 --> 00:29:25.029
AG: Afterward, Jane leads a discussion
asking what worked for people.

00:29:25.053 --> 00:29:27.783
JD: And I say, "OK, now
you each give one each other

00:29:27.807 --> 00:29:32.296
one piece of feedback
about what you saw worked